In article <dpn2.173.723545554@po.CWRU.Edu> dpn2@po.CWRU.Edu (Damien P. Neil) writes:

   >Do giant spiders always confer Poison resistance when you eat them, or 
   >does this only happen some times?

   I've eaten every spider corpse I've come across, and have yet to get it. It 
   seems to be rather rare -- I have better luck with gray ooze.

From what I remember, cave spiders may give you that poison resistance
without being poisonous, which is a neat advantage. However, don't
count on it, the probability is very low.

   >If I ever get lucky enough to find another magic lamp, I want to wish for 
   >a device that will give me more wishes.  Is there such a device, and what 
   >is it called (exact spelling please), or should I just wish for 10 blessed 
   >scrolls of recharging?

   "I wish I never wished a wand of wishing -- wishful thinking."
   Don't wish for things that can give you wishes -- ask for 3 blessed scrolls 
   of charging. (Do they work on lamps? Maybe not...)

   Never wish for more than three of a thing, or a thing with more than three 
   plusses. You won't get it.

You may actually wish for three scrolls and three potions. That may work,
and wishing for two of the above almost certainly works.

   >I am playing a 7th level priest in a dungeon full of altars to Crom.  
   >Everytime I offer something, I get the following message:  "You have a 
   >feeling of inadequacy."  I did anger Crom once by praying too soon.  What
   >is the problem?

   He's mad at you. Offer more, and he'll finally relent.

It's not enough to offer MORE, you have to offer BETTER, that is,
monsters with a higher class. The formulae for this is (as I remember
it, at least) a bit complicated. Perhaps somebody could post a list of
what monsters that works. (Obvious conclusion: if you offer one rothe,
and it doesn't help, it won't help with 10 rothes.) (Obvious
conclusion II: if your corpse does work, make a mental note so that
you know until the next time this happens.)

   >How do I reverse the effects of the very nasty potion of halucination?  
   >I've tried waiting it out, but some pissant halucination distorted 
   >something or other usually kills me.

   I think praying will work, if you are in good favor with your god. But why 
   bother? It's fun to hallucinate -- you get the best messages that way. Just 
   be careful about what you attack, and be ready to run.

The easiest way is to get a unicorn horn. A blessed or uncursed
unicorn horn cures blinding, sicknes, confusion, stunning and
hallucination, one at a time, whan applied. If you ar for instance
both  stunned and confused, simply apply it twice. Note that if your
unicorn horn is cursed you instead get worse.

